e this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-based district that leans Democratic by about two points, with a favorable national environment adding to her edge. Most expert raters call the race Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price her chances around 95 percent.\n\nRepublican Carrie Buck has proven to be a serious challenger, raising more than Titus and drawing national support, including visits from Speaker Mike Johnson and Education Secretary McMahon. Still, without public polling and with Titus's incumbency advantage, the race remains Likely Democratic rather than a true tossup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9451, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9504, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9234, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9304, "margin": 10.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9333, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9462, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9326, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9428, "margi